Translation patch: `GnoInterval::check_and_new`

Change: `io::Error::new(InvalidData, format!("start({}) >= end({}) in GnoInterval", start, end))` becomes `misc::trusted::gno_interval_order_error(start, end)` (a new function of the module of patch 64 whose body is that expression), and `io::Error::new(InvalidData, "Gno can't be zero")` becomes `misc::io_error_msg(InvalidData, "Gno can't be zero")` (patch 02).
Why: Aeneas does not support `dyn` (inside `io::Error::new`) or `format!`.
Behaviour: Identical: the same errors are built at the same points.

diff --git a/src/misc/trusted.rs b/src/misc/trusted.rs
index 65c6fff..23773cc 100644
--- a/src/misc/trusted.rs
+++ b/src/misc/trusted.rs
@@ -18,6 +18,14 @@ pub(crate) fn from_utf8_lossy(bytes: &[u8]) -> Cow<'_, str> {
     String::from_utf8_lossy(bytes)
 }
 
+/// The error of `GnoInterval::check_and_new` for `start >= end`.
+pub(crate) fn gno_interval_order_error(start: u64, end: u64) -> std::io::Error {
+    std::io::Error::new(
+        std::io::ErrorKind::InvalidData,
+        format!("start({}) >= end({}) in GnoInterval", start, end),
+    )
+}
+
